      <marc:subfield code="a">This book explains the basic outline of the New Testament books, the context in which they were written (author, target audience, time, place, and purpose), and the characteristics of the books. In addition to this, it adds &quot;Questions to Ponder,&quot; &quot;Sharing and Discussion,&quot; &quot;Life Reflection,&quot; &quot;Review,&quot; &quot;Golden Words,&quot; and &quot;Extended Reading.&quot;  The purpose of this book is to serve not only as a resource for Christians to read, study, think and reflect, but also as a material for brothers and sisters to read, discuss and share together in church groups.</marc:subfield>
